<title>UK: Energy deal gets regulator's okay - paper.</title>
<headline>Energy deal gets regulator's okay - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stephen Littlechild, the electricity industry regulator, has decided against raising serious regulatory objections to the proposed 3.7 billion takeover of Energy Group Plc by PacifiCorp of the U.S., the Independent said on Monday.</p>
<p>Executives from the two companies held talks with Littlechild at his offices on Friday.</p>
<p>Littlechild's advice will put further pressure on the Department of Trade and Industry to let the deal go through without a referral to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission, the paper said. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
